# Store shell scripts with LF endings, always.
#
# A CRLF shebang makes bash fail on Linux with "bad interpreter: No such file
# or directory" - which in a cron log looks like the script never ran at all.
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, so without this rule a Windows checkout
# plus a copy to a Linux box is enough to reintroduce it.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
